Fedora Workstation Live @RELEASE@ for Microsoft Surface Pro 11 (Snapdragon X Elite, OLED, incl. 5G SKU)

Kernel:        @ABI@ (ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11 @COMMIT@, mode: @MODE@); the stock Fedora kernel is not offered.
Device tree:   @DTB@ (loaded explicitly by GRUB; installed system uses GRUB_DEVICETREE in BLS entries)
Built:         @DATE@ for SKU @SKU@
Base media:    @MEDIA@
Secure Boot:   must be DISABLED (unsigned kernel).

Live session:  Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, GPU acceleration, touch and pen work. Audio and battery status are
               unavailable on the live USB because the audio DSP is kept off while booting from USB-C
               (modprobe.blacklist=qcom_q6v5_pas). They work after installation to the internal disk.

Installation:  run "Install to Hard Drive". The installed system boots this kernel with the Denali DTB;
               a one-shot service (sp11-first-boot) removes the live-only DSP blacklist on the first boot.

RPMs used to build this media are under /sp11/rpms.

Redistribution: this media and the RPMs under /sp11/rpms contain proprietary Qualcomm firmware copied
               from the Windows installation of the machine that built it. Do not pass them on; build
               your own from the source repository instead.
Credits:       kernel ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11 (GPL-2.0); audio topology, UCM and pen integration
               from ooaklee/linux-surface-pro-11-oe; iptsd from linux-surface/iptsd; Fedora Workstation Live.
